Use the module "math.tell" as math.
Use the module "lists.tell" as lists.
Use the module "text.tell" as texts.
Use the module "statistics.tell" as stats.

Check that math.clamp(-1, 0, 10) is equal to 0.
Check that math.clamp(5, 0, 10) is equal to 5.
Check that math.clamp(11, 0, 10) is equal to 10.
Check that math.lerp(10, 20, 0.5) is equal to 15.
Check that [math.sign(-5), math.sign(0), math.sign(5)] is equal to [-1, 0, 1].

Let items be [1, 2, 3].
Let chunks be lists.chunked(items, 2).
Check that chunks is equal to [[1, 2], [3]].
Set items[0] to 99.
Check that chunks[0][0] is equal to 1.
Check that lists.chunked([], 2) is equal to [].
Check that lists.chunked([1, 2], 100000000000000000000) is equal to [[1, 2]].
Check that lists.flatten([[1], [], [2, 3]]) is equal to [1, 2, 3].
Check that lists.zip(["a", "b"], [1]) is equal to [["a", 1]].
Check that lists.zip([], [1]) is equal to [].

Check that texts.starts_with("東京🙂", "東").
Check that texts.ends_with("東京🙂", "京🙂").
Check that texts.starts_with("", "").
Check that texts.ends_with("東京🙂", "").
Check that not texts.ends_with("🙂", "京🙂").
Check that not texts.starts_with("Tell", "tell").
Check that texts.join(["", "東京", ""], "|") is equal to "|東京|".
Check that texts.join([], "|") is equal to "".

Let scores be [11, 3, 9].
Check that stats.median(scores) is equal to 9.
Check that scores is equal to [11, 3, 9].
Check that stats.median([9, 3, 5, 7]) is equal to 6.
Check that stats.median([-10, 4]) is equal to -3.

Let caught be false.
Try:
    lists.chunked([1], 1.5).
If something goes wrong:
    Set caught to true.
End try.
Check that caught.

Set caught to false.
Try:
    stats.median([]).
If something goes wrong:
    Set caught to true.
End try.
Check that caught.
